    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "e93603846ce9af7b540c617fe47b8db9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"1-duplicate-card-payments-from-a-delta-table\">1. Duplicate card payments, from a Delta table</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Say you're on the payments team. A customer was charged twice for the\nsame coffee, and by the time support hears about it, they've already\ntweeted. You want to catch these <strong>double charges</strong>, the same card\npaying the same amount at the same merchant twice within five minutes,\nand refund them first.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The rule comes from the <a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/v0.3.0/catalogue/INDEX.md\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">query catalogue</a>\n(<code>fin-duplicate-payments</code>); stream processors write it as an interval\njoin, and here it is a self-join on a Delta Lake table of card\ntransactions. The refund queue trusts what you hand it, so it has to be\nright: no pair twice, no charge matched with itself, and nothing left\nover when a charge is reversed.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We'll go through the whole job:</span>\n<ol>\n<li>read the transactions from a Delta table, with its Change Data Feed;</li>\n<li>write the rule in Ibis and state its <strong>contract</strong>: what it assumes\n   about the input, and what the refund queue may rely on;</li>\n<li>have the contract <strong>proved</strong> before any data runs;</li>\n<li>run the same checked plan on DuckDB, Polars and DataFusion, and write\n   it as Snowflake and Spark SQL;</li>\n<li><strong>maintain the result from the change feed</strong> when new transactions\n   arrive and old ones are reversed, and see what the usual \"process\n   the new rows\" job gets wrong;</li>\n<li>write it to a Delta table that carries the contract, so the next job\n   can build on it.</li>\n</ol></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "8c33c64911cb5ac40218de466022bf4d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"1-the-source-a-delta-table-of-transactions\">1. The source: a Delta table of transactions</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Amounts are integer cents: money as DOUBLE does not compare exactly, and\nan equality of amounts is the whole rule. The table has the Change Data\nFeed on (so later runs can read what changed) and a CHECK constraint\nthat amounts are not negative. The data has one real double charge, a\nnear miss on card 11 half an hour apart, and card 12, whose two payments\narrived without a merchant at all.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
