    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "1c7b4061d0ba2126499b64a7f4840831",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>postcondition</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>unique(first_txn, duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_txn &lt; _.duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>_.merchant.notnull()</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.amount_cents &gt;= 0)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_ts &lt;= _.duplicate_ts)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>output column</th>\n<th>known values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>card_id</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merchant</code></td>\n<td>a string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>amount_cents</code></td>\n<td>an integer \u2265 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "9d4cc8bb8dc55f6a566b8a5b2909a627",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Every postcondition is \u2705 proved, and no runtime error is possible. How\neach one follows:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>unique(first_txn, duplicate_txn)</code></strong>: <code>txn_id</code> is a key of the\n  input, so a pair of ids identifies a pair of rows.</li>\n<li><strong><code>merchant</code> is never NULL</strong>, although the column is nullable: rows\n  only join when <code>a.merchant = b.merchant</code> is TRUE, and <code>NULL = NULL</code> is\n  not. Card 12's payments never match. (pandas' <code>merge</code> <em>does</em> match\n  NaN with NaN, and a Polars join does with <code>nulls_equal=True</code>: a port\n  of this rule to a dataframe library can change its result.)</li>\n<li><strong><code>first_ts &lt;= duplicate_ts</code></strong> comes from the join condition, which\n  holds on every output row.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Each precondition was established without trusting anyone's word for\nit, and the first refresh says how:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "6e924dd06505742dacb11461401add9c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[\"transactions: unique(txn_id) (checked on data)\", \"transactions: (_.amount_cents >= 0) (Delta constraint)\", \"transactions: (_.ts < datetime.datetime(2100, 1, 1, 0, 0)) (file stats @v1)\"]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "8ee955f2d0d2854e58abebda4a7a0703",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The amount bound comes from the table's <strong>Delta CHECK constraint</strong>, the\ntimestamp bound from the <strong>file statistics</strong> (the maximum <code>ts</code> of each\nfile), and the key is checked on the data, since Delta doesn't enforce\nkeys. A later batch only checks the files it added.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The node holds the one double charge in the data, and neither the near\nmiss nor card 12's merchant-less pair:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "iLit",
      "code_hash": "fc780e700e42f988e5290c3aa2099b1d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>duplicate_payments</strong></span></span><table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>card_id</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>merchant</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>amount_cents</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_ts</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_ts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>1</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>10</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>coffee</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>450</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 08:00</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 08:02</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "83529cc2ad05741b0554d9be22e9833e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"break-the-rule\">Break the rule</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The easiest bug in a self-join is forgetting that a row matches itself,\nand the customer would find out first: every payment refunded as its own\nduplicate. Switch off <code>a.txn_id &lt; b.txn_id</code> (or loosen it to <code>&lt;=</code>) and\nthe contract is re-checked:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "4b80bb040ec206b5e152a39550fecb77",
      "outputs": [
