    {
      "id": "Pvdt",
      "code_hash": "cfc956ef39ce671e72f4fff16fddcec9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-new-transactions-keeping-the-result-up-to-date\">4. New transactions: keeping the result up to date</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">An hour later, two things have happened to the source table:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>transaction 7 arrived late: card 11 paid 25.99 for books at 09:03, a\n  duplicate of transaction <strong>3</strong>, which was loaded in the first run;</li>\n<li>transaction 2 was <strong>reversed</strong> and deleted, so the coffee pair is no\n  longer a double charge.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZBYS",
      "code_hash": "4a0d5c15880b512113b357ddd8a36b43",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "{\"num_added_files\": 2, \"num_removed_files\": 1, \"num_deleted_rows\": 1, \"num_copied_rows\": 5, \"execution_time_ms\": 6, \"scan_time_ms\": 2, \"rewrite_time_ms\": 0}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "f06ee6c45d8f90363307fc08a43b484c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"the-usual-incremental-job\">The usual incremental job</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The common way to avoid recomputing the self-join is a watermark: find\nthe duplicates among the rows that arrived since the last run, and\nappend them to the output. It runs fast, and it is wrong twice, once\nfor each of the two changes:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "f933bbfb27e977c120354850f7c9c27e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[[1, 2]]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "4dc85ec3b1e76631708d5858a82da7c4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">It <strong>misses (3, 7)</strong>, because transaction 3 is not among the new rows,\nand it <strong>keeps (1, 2)</strong>, because an append-only job never sees the\nreversal, so that customer gets a refund for a charge that no longer\nexists. Fixing that by hand means joining the new rows with the old\nones both ways, and handling deletes and updates: that is the delta rule\nof a join, <code>\u0394(A \u22c8 B) = \u0394A \u22c8 (B + \u0394B) + A \u22c8 \u0394B</code>, and it is easy to get\nsubtly wrong.</span>\n<h3 id=\"the-nodes-refresh\">The node's refresh</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>dups.refresh()</code> reads the Change Data Feed from the version the node\nwas computed at, checks the preconditions on the new rows only, and\nruns the delta plans Lean derived and <strong>proved</strong> to give the same result\nas a full recompute:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "AjVT",
      "code_hash": "337cf4bb3700ff4a5d10b91fecb9bc17",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "duplicate_payments:\n  transactions@v1\u2192v3: 1 insert(s), 1 delete(s); \u0394 trusted as coming from Delta CDF v1\u2192v3\n  requires transactions: (_.amount_cents >= 0) (Delta constraint)\n  requires transactions: (_.ts < datetime.datetime(2100, 1, 1, 0, 0)) (file stats @v3 (new files))\n  requires transactions: unique(txn_id) (checked on data)\n  view duplicate_payments: transactions@v3\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pHFh",
      "code_hash": "cc75b8d7449f5aa21a54d8b261d2d608",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>duplicate_payments after the refresh</strong></span></span><table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>card_id</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>merchant</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>amount_cents</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_ts</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_ts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>3</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>7</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>11</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>books</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2599</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 09:00</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 09:03</td></tr></tbody></table></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The late duplicate is found and the reversed pair is gone, and the node holds the same rows as a new one computed from scratch.</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NCOB",
      "code_hash": "dcb1a4d2e125242e71abaa181f1033c3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The report names the one thing the proof takes on trust: that the\nchange feed really turns the old snapshot into the new one (\"\u0394 trusted\nas coming from Delta CDF\"). Where the feed is gone (CDF off, files\nvacuumed), the refresh diffs the two snapshots instead, and says so.\n<code>dups.refresh(audit=True)</code> also compares every batch with a recompute\nbefore it is applied.</span>\n<h2 id=\"5-the-sink-carries-the-contract\">5. The sink carries the contract</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>dups.write(DeltaSink(...))</code> stores the node in a Delta table, and every\nrefresh writes it <strong>exactly once per state</strong>: the commit is keyed by the\nsource versions, so a retried job can't write a batch twice. The first\nwrite creates the table; the proved guarantees become NOT NULL columns\nand CHECK constraints, and the commit metadata records the plan and the\ncontract. Later writes MERGE only the change.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
